%% Kerberos SMB mount of an Azure file share from a Contoso workstation - name resolution, ticket, share RBAC, NTFS ACL - Contoso profile
%% Source: codex/playbook-enable-identity-based-auth-ad-ds.md and codex/blueprint-azure-files-private-endpoint.md (Microsoft Learn: On-premises AD DS authentication for Azure Files; Assign share-level permissions; Configure directory and file-level permissions; Enable AD DS authentication)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant WS as Domain-joined workstation on contoso.local
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant RES as DNS Private Resolver inbound endpoint in the hub
  participant DC as Contoso domain controller
  participant PE as Private endpoint file sub-resource in the spoke
  participant AF as Azure Files service
  participant ARM as Azure RBAC share role assignments
  Note over WS,AF: Step A - resolve the name to a private IP before any SMB packet is sent
  WS->>IB: stmtyfiles01.file.core.windows.net A record ?
  IB->>IB: public DNS returns CNAME to stmtyfiles01.privatelink.file.core.windows.net
  IB->>RES: forward privatelink.file.core.windows.net to the inbound endpoint
  RES-->>IB: A 10.x.x.x from the private DNS zone
  IB-->>WS: A 10.x.x.x
  Note over WS,DC: Step B - Kerberos, entirely on Contoso network, no Azure involvement
  WS->>DC: AS-REQ, user already holds a TGT for CONTOSO.LOCAL
  WS->>DC: TGS-REQ for SPN cifs/stmtyfiles01.file.core.windows.net
  DC-->>WS: service ticket encrypted with the AD object password, AES-256, PAC carries every group SID
  Note over WS,AF: Step C - SMB 445 over ExpressRoute private peering to the private endpoint
  WS->>PE: SMB3.1.1 session setup on TCP 445 with the service ticket
  PE->>AF: forwarded on the Microsoft backbone, never over the public endpoint
  AF->>AF: decrypt the ticket with the kerb key, read the user SID and group SIDs
  AF->>ARM: does any SID map to a synced Entra group with a share-level role ?
  alt a synced group holds Storage File Data SMB Share Contributor
    ARM-->>AF: gate 1 passed, share-level read write delete
    AF->>AF: gate 2, evaluate the NTFS DACL on the directory and file
    AF-->>WS: effective access is the MOST RESTRICTIVE of gate 1 and gate 2
    WS->>WS: klist shows a cifs ticket, Get-SmbConnection shows the 10.x private IP
  else no role assignment and defaultSharePermission is None
    ARM-->>AF: gate 1 failed
    AF-->>WS: access denied at share level, the NTFS ACL is never consulted
    Note over WS,ARM: fix is a role assignment to the AD-synced GROUP, or a default share-level permission for non-synced principals such as computer accounts, sMSA and gMSA
  end
  Note over WS,AF: Failure branches seen in the field
  alt AD object password expired or the UPN does not match the SPN
    DC-->>WS: error 1396 target account name is incorrect, KRB_AP_ERR_MODIFIED
    WS->>WS: repair with Update-AzStorageAccountADObjectPassword -RotateToKerbKey kerb2, then klist purge
  else the object is still on RC4 after the July 2026 Windows Server default change to AES-256
    DC-->>WS: ticket the storage account cannot validate, mount fails
    WS->>WS: repair with Set-ADComputer -KerberosEncryptionType AES256, then klist purge and remount
  else DNS returned a public IP instead of 10.x
    WS-->>WS: the mount leaves ExpressRoute or is blocked by the storage firewall Deny rule
  end
